  "scope_corrections": [
    "The candidate4 all48 AOT lock audit covered static project closure and package equality. It did not prove evaluated lock selection or actual AOT restore consistency; the later selector review explicitly preserves this correction.",
    "Candidate5/6 Host failure diagnosis was corrected before mutation: committed AOT locks already contained Linux RID and pinned SDK compiler/linker entries. Candidate6 changes three selectors only; all129 lock bytes remain unchanged from candidate5.",
    "Candidate5 rustfmt adds the formatter optional trailing call-argument comma as well as line wrapping; token equivalence is claimed modulo that optional comma, not literal whitespace-only equality.",
    "Candidate4 targeted provider runs and candidate3 API reruns retain their original source and author attribution. They are not clean candidate6 full-pipeline or package acceptance.",
    "Inherited runner cleanup guarantees are unchanged and scoped to the preserved review; no additional process-group/SIGKILL/startup-failure guarantee is invented."
  ],
